</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Table <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 5.1 SSL Backbone Selection ‣ 5 Results ‣ From Self-Supervised Speech Models to Mixture-of-Experts for Robust Anti-Spoofing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, the 13-layer configuration achieves better performance for WavLM-Large, supporting this choice.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T3.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="S5.T3.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Detailed anti-spoofing results (EER <math id="S5.T3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math>, in %) with Codec = Codecfake and LSV = LibriSeVoc. The <span id="S5.T3.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MoE Config</span> columns specify the insertion position (first 6, last 6, all 13, or alternating), the number of experts <math id="S5.T3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>, the top-<math id="S5.T3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> value, and the pooling strategy (att = attentive, stat = statistical). Macro EER averages EERs across corpora; Micro EER pools all trials. Best in <span id="S5.T3.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span>, second-best <span id="S5.T3.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">underlined</span>.</span></figcaption>
<div id="S5.T3.8" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:98.3pt;vertical-align:-48.3pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-316.8pt,90.3pt) scale(0.352565861321369,0.352565861321369) ;">
